    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"duckspatial: new geometry functions, MVT/MBTiles export, and more\"\ndescription: \"Highlights from duckspatial v1.1.2 and v1.2.0\"\ndate: \"2026-07-04\"\ncategories: [R, spatial, duckspatial]\nimage: \"image.png\"\nexecute: \n  warning: false\neditor_options: \n  chunk_output_type: console\n---\n\n## Introduction\n\nTwo versions of {duckspatial} have shipped since the last update: v1.1.2 and v1.2.0. Both are now on CRAN, so let's go through the highlights together.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-fold=\"true\" code-summary=\"Load packages and data\"}\n## Packages setup\n# pak::pak(\"duckspatial\") # upgrade the package to the latest version\nlibrary(dplyr)\nlibrary(duckspatial)\nlibrary(ggplot2)\nlibrary(mapgl)\nlibrary(sf)\n\n## Load some data\nargentina_ddbs <- ddbs_open_dataset(\n  system.file(\"spatial/argentina.geojson\", package = \"duckspatial\")\n)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## New geometry functions\n\nA batch of new unary functions covers common needs that weren't in the package yet.\n\n::: panel-tabset\n\n## ddbs_reverse\n\nThis function flips the vertex order of a geometry.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nddbs_reverse(argentina_ddbs)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A duckspatial lazy spatial table\n# ● CRS: EPSG:4326 \n# ● Geometry column: geom \n# ● Geometry type: POLYGON \n# ● Bounding box: xmin: -73.525 ymin: -52.398 xmax: -53.624 ymax: -21.818 \n# Data backed by DuckDB (dbplyr lazy evaluation)\n# Use ddbs_collect() or st_as_sf() to materialize to sf\n#\n# Source:   table<temp_table_eda21e35_a697_4ac7_aff0_b34404274264> [?? x 8]\n# Database: DuckDB 1.5.4 [cidre@Linux 7.0.0-22-generic:R 4.6.0/:memory:]\n  OGC_FID CNTR_ID NAME_ENGL ISO3_CODE CNTR_NAME FID   date       geom           \n    <dbl> <chr>   <chr>     <chr>     <chr>     <chr> <date>     <wk_wkb>       \n1       0 AR      Argentina ARG       Argentina AR    2021-01-01 <POLYGON ((-62…\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## ddbs_normalize\n\nIt returns the canonical form of the geometry, sorting the geometry in a deterministic way. This is useful before comparing geometries for equality.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nddbs_normalize(argentina_ddbs)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A duckspatial lazy spatial table\n# ● CRS: EPSG:4326 \n# ● Geometry column: geom \n# ● Geometry type: POLYGON \n# ● Bounding box: xmin: -73.525 ymin: -52.398 xmax: -53.624 ymax: -21.818 \n# Data backed by DuckDB (dbplyr lazy evaluation)\n# Use ddbs_collect() or st_as_sf() to materialize to sf\n#\n# Source:   table<temp_table_6c5d7a2b_7430_4d40_8114_c5de5ac10f25> [?? x 8]\n# Database: DuckDB 1.5.4 [cidre@Linux 7.0.0-22-generic:R 4.6.0/:memory:]\n  OGC_FID CNTR_ID NAME_ENGL ISO3_CODE CNTR_NAME FID   date       geom           \n    <dbl> <chr>   <chr>     <chr>     <chr>     <chr> <date>     <wk_wkb>       \n1       0 AR      Argentina ARG       Argentina AR    2021-01-01 <POLYGON ((-73…\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## ddbs_vertices\n\nCollects every vertex of a geometry into a MULTIPOINT.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nargentina_vertices_sf <- ddbs_vertices(argentina_ddbs, mode = \"sf\")\nmaplibre_view(argentina_vertices_sf)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-8f75cdec4b8a6a2e8d95\" style=\"width:100%;height:480px;\" class=\"maplibregl html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-8f75cdec4b8a6a2e8d95\">{\"x\":{\"style\":\"https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/gl/positron-gl-style/style.json\",\"center\":[0,0],\"zoom\":0,\"bearing\":0,\"pitch\":0,\"projection\":\"globe\",\"additional_params\":{\"bounds\":[-73.52455,-52.39754999744891,-53.62409,-21.8179299858344]},\"setProjection\":[{\"projection\":\"globe\"}],\"layers\":[{\"id\":\"quickview\",\"type\":\"circle\",\"source\":{\"type\":\"geojson\",\"data\":{\"type\":\"FeatureCollection\",\"features\":[{\"type\":\"Feature\",\"properties\":{\"OGC_FID\":0.0,\"CNTR_ID\":\"AR\",\"NAME_ENGL\":